  "transcript": "Amazon's growth engine is one of the most famous flywheels in business. Let's break it down using stocks and flows. It starts with the customer base — Prime members. As customers grow, they generate more traffic. More traffic attracts third-party sellers onto the marketplace. Those sellers bring new product listings, expanding the overall product selection. A wider selection improves the customer experience. But there's another force at work: scale. More volume means lower cost structure, which enables lower prices. Lower prices and better experience both drive new member signups, feeding the customer base again. This is the virtuous cycle that turned an online bookstore into the everything store.",
